<!-- The geometries of both heads (2026-11-10, the user's choice): the drawings the WPF tree rows, toolbar and menus
     show, and the Avalonia head too, which builds its Themes/Icons.axaml from this file at build (Build/SharedXaml.targets)
     as it builds its string tables; the path markup is the same in both frameworks. Since 2026-11-11 every keyed geometry
     of the two heads is here (the user's report: the transport bar's glyphs, the pictures' handles, the tree's and the
     forms' buttons and the chrome's arrows had stood in each head's panes and themes, the port's copies of the WPF ones):
     a pane or a theme of either head declares none of its own and names these by key, the WPF head through Controls.xaml,
     which merges this file, the Avalonia head through its application's resources. The icons are 16 px, 1 px strokes on
     half pixels, ink in rows and columns 0 to 14 (odd, so it centres like text); a shape that is filled has a second
     geometry with the Fill suffix. The 40 of the menus, the folders and the forms replaced the Segoe Fluent glyphs the WPF
     head had used, which Linux and macOS have not (2026-11-10, the user's choice of drawings over an icon font). -->
